  '{"event_name":"Summer Fancy Food Show 2026","event_url":"https://www.specialtyfood.com/fancy-food-shows/summer/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"original_line":25,"dates":"June 28-30, 2026","location":"New York, NY","cost":"Booth costs approximately $5,500 USD for 10x10 pipe and drape; attendee badges vary by registration type","venue":"Jacob K. Javits Convention Center","description":"The specialty food industry''s premier product discovery and networking event for makers, buyers, distributors, brokers, press, and foodservice professionals. Now in its 70th year, it is one of the food industry''s tentpole events and North America''s largest specialty food trade show with nearly 2,500 brands exhibiting and more than 900 new products on display.","industry_vertical":"food_supply","exhibitor_mix":"Specialty food and beverage manufacturers, artisanal food producers, gourmet brands, international food suppliers, organic and natural food companies, plant-based food innovators, confectionery makers, cheese producers, coffee and tea suppliers, snack manufacturers, and emerging specialty food brands from over 57 countries","audience_mix":"Approximately 47,000 specialty food professionals including retail buyers from supermarkets, independent grocers, club stores, specialty and natural food stores, e-commerce buyers, restaurateurs, food service distributors, wholesale distributors, importers, distributors, brokers, press, and foodservice professionals","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":null,"original_event_name":"The SFA Summer Fancy Food Show","original_event_url":"https://www.specialtyfood.com/fancy-food-shows/summer/","added_to_master":"2026-03-31T11:49:29.130780","master_id":55,"overall_score":6.2,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":8,"rationale":"Strong alignment with distribution vertical. Audience includes food distributors (wholesale distributors, regional distributors, importers, brokers) managing product discovery, inventory, and buyer relationships. Food service distributors and foodservice professionals are explicit InstaLILY ICP. Sales operations and distribution management heavily represented."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":7,"rationale":"Large established event (June 28-30, 2026, New York). 47,000 attendees with 2,500 brands exhibiting - massive scale. Jacob K. Javits Convention Center accessible venue. June timing moderate but event is 70 years established. Confirmed dates."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":5,"rationale":"Audience includes retail buyers, e-commerce buyers, restaurateurs, and foodservice distributors - mix of mid-level and senior buying roles. While decision-makers present, event skews toward procurement and product discovery rather than C-suite operations/sales leadership focused on workflow automation."}},"reasoning":"Fancy Food Show has strong distribution and food supply alignment but moderate InstaLILY fit. Event is primarily product discovery and procurement marketplace rather than operations/technology conference. Buyers attend to source products, not to evaluate operational AI platforms. Large scale (47,000) and relevant buyer functions (distributors, foodservice) are positive, but event format (trade show vs. conference) and buyer intent (sourcing vs. operations improvement) reduce effectiveness.","sales_brief":"MODERATE PRIORITY - Food/specialty distribution is ICP vertical and 47,000 attendees includes key buyer functions (foodservice distributors, wholesale distributors, importers). June timing good. However, event format is product discovery trade show, not operations/technology conference - buyers focused on sourcing products, not evaluating workflow automation solutions. Possible for sponsorship/booth visibility but likely lower ROI than dedicated operations/technology events. Better targeting through industry-specific supply chain conferences."}'::jsonb
