. However, event emphasis on innovation showcase and content creation may attract enthusiasts and technical buyers vs. C-suite. Mix includes automotive shop owners and racing teams which are lower-authority buyers. Seniority distribution likely skews toward mid-level rather than executive."}},"reasoning":"HPX serves automotive aftermarket, a subsegment of broader automotive ICP. Event is new and unproven, presenting risk around attendee quality and decision-maker concentration. While performance parts distributors and retailers have operational challenges (quoting, inventory management across multi-location networks), this niche is narrower than broader automotive, industrial, or construction supply distributors. New event status and emphasis on innovation/women empowerment suggests attendee mix may skew toward early adopters and networking vs. active procurement. Better alternatives exist in broader automotive and industrial verticals.","sales_brief":"Secondary consideration - emerging event in automotive aftermarket niche. Performance parts distributors present but vertical is narrower than core automotive ICP. New event status creates uncertainty on attendee quality and decision-maker concentration. June timing acceptable. Risk: Innovation-focused agenda may attract fewer operations executives with budget authority vs. technical enthusiasts. Recommend low-resource reconnaissance attendance only; wait for event maturity before major investment."}'::jsonb
