  '{"event_name":"NAFA 2026 Institute & Expo","event_url":"https://www.nafainstitute.org/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"April 13-15, 2026","location":"Cleveland, OH","cost":"Varies by registration date, role, and NAFA membership","venue":"Huntington Convention Center of Cleveland","description":"The fleet industry''s premier event featuring three days of unparalleled education with 60+ sessions, networking, and exhibits from 230+ leading suppliers. Attracts 2,100+ fleet professionals from corporate, government, public safety, utility, and education sectors. Co-located with Conference of Automotive Remarketing.","industry_vertical":"automotives","exhibitor_mix":"Fleet management software providers, vehicle OEMs, telematics and GPS tracking vendors, fuel management solutions, fleet maintenance services, electric vehicle suppliers, fleet leasing companies, parts and service providers, insurance companies, and emerging fleet technology innovators","audience_mix":"Fleet managers, directors of fleet operations, transportation managers, procurement specialists, sustainability officers, and decision-makers from corporate fleets, government agencies, public safety departments, utilities, educational institutions managing vehicle fleets of all types","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Complete information found. NAFA has 60+ years of advancing the fleet profession. Conference includes OEM panel discussion, Innovations Showcase, and new NAFA Garage hands-on area.","original_event_name":"NAFA 2026 Institute & Expo","original_event_url":"https://www.nafainstitute.org/","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:34:50.627175","master_id":49,"overall_score":3.4,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":4,"rationale":"Fleet management is distinct function from sales and operations. Fleet managers, directors of fleet operations, and transportation managers focus on vehicle acquisition, maintenance, fuel, and logistics optimization. While they manage operations, they are not in sales or distribution contexts that drive InstaLILY use cases. Procurement specialists present but not aligned with InstaLILY quoting, sales velocity, or parts knowledge problems."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":7,"rationale":"April 2026 timing ideal. Established annual event with 2,100+ fleet professionals. Cleveland venue accessible. Three-day format with 60+ sessions indicates substantial educational content. Proven industry standard with 60+ years of operation."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":6,"rationale":"Directors and managers of fleet operations have decision-making authority but focus is fleet procurement and operations, not technology platform adoption for sales/operations workflows. Some sustainability officers and procurement specialists present. Mid-level management present but not concentrated in roles aligned with InstaLILY buying authority."}},"reasoning":"NAFA 2026 does not align with InstaLILY ICP despite automotive vertical mention. Fleet management is operationally distinct from InstaLILY target customers (distributors, suppliers, field-service companies). Fleet managers deal with vehicle acquisition, maintenance contracts, fuel optimization, and telematics - not parts inventory management, sales quoting, or multi-location sales operations. Automotive vertical in InstaLILY context means automotive goods distributors (parts suppliers), not fleet operators. Event audience is not positioned to evaluate solutions for InstaLILY pain points.","sales_brief":"Low priority - Wrong buyer context. NAFA serves fleet operations (vehicle management), not automotive goods distributors or parts suppliers. Fleet managers buying fleet software is distinct from multi-location distribution executives managing sales teams and parts knowledge. Minimal overlap with InstaLILY ICP verticals and use cases."}'::jsonb
