  '855daaee-72da-5147-bf5b-ff35da0fffe3',
  'TIA Capital Ideas Conference 2026',
  'https://web.cvent.com/event/5fcaa2f1-f19b-4e81-a814-d17aa1a29d03/websitePage:fe4fb1cb-f5ba-4897-a32c-606d09490169',
  'web.cvent.com/event/5fcaa2f1-f19b-4e81-a814-d17aa1a29d03/websitepage:fe4fb1cb-f5ba-4897-a32c-606d09490169',
  'April 15-18, 2026',
  '2026-04-15',
  '2026-04-18',
  'Phoenix, AZ',
  'JW Marriott Phoenix Desert Ridge Resort & Spa',
  null,
  'The only meeting dedicated to third-party logistics providers, bringing together 1,500+ of North America''s most successful brokerage-based logistics professionals for four days of networking, education, and reconnecting. Features 5+ general sessions, 24+ education sessions, 50+ learning lab breakouts, and exhibit hall with 70+ vendors.',
  'supply_chain_and_distribution',
  'Transportation management software providers, freight technology platforms, load boards and matching services, insurance and risk management companies, factoring and financial services, tracking and visibility solutions, compliance and regulatory technology, carrier management systems, and logistics consulting firms',
  'Freight brokers, 3PL executives, owners and senior managers of logistics companies, operations managers, sales leaders, business development professionals, and decision-makers from third-party logistics providers and transportation intermediaries across North America',
  'enriched',
  6.9,
  'TIA Capital Ideas Conference is meaningful opportunity despite outside traditional InstaLILY core verticals. The event targets asset-light 3PLs and freight brokers - exactly the supply chain vertical identified in Criteria Set B as highest alignment. These companies operate high-volume, multi-stakeholder workflows managing load assignment, carrier communication, and customer matching - operationally similar to InstaLILY distribution use cases around order routing and exception handling. However, InstaLILY has not demonstrated explicit freight brokerage or 3PL success stories. Event represents adjacent expansion opportunity rather than core vertical play. April timing and senior manager concentration (owners with buying authority) indicate quality attendees.',
  'Secondary expansion opportunity - Asset-light 3PLs and freight brokers face similar workflow complexity to InstaLILY distribution customers (high-volume, multi-step, exception-handling). 1,500+ attendees with owner and senior manager concentration = decision-maker density. April timing optimal. TIA represents $343B industry with mature buyer awareness. Risk: Vertical is adjacent to core InstaLILY verticals with no public customer reference. May require education on applicability of distribution-focused InstaWorkers platform to logistics workflows.',
  '{"event_name":"TIA Capital Ideas Conference 2026","event_url":"https://web.cvent.com/event/5fcaa2f1-f19b-4e81-a814-d17aa1a29d03/websitePage:fe4fb1cb-f5ba-4897-a32c-606d09490169","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"April 15-18, 2026","location":"Phoenix, AZ","cost":null,"venue":"JW Marriott Phoenix Desert Ridge Resort & Spa","description":"The only meeting dedicated to third-party logistics providers, bringing together 1,500+ of North America''s most successful brokerage-based logistics professionals for four days of networking, education, and reconnecting. Features 5+ general sessions, 24+ education sessions, 50+ learning lab breakouts, and exhibit hall with 70+ vendors.","industry_vertical":"supply_chain_and_distribution","exhibitor_mix":"Transportation management software providers, freight technology platforms, load boards and matching services, insurance and risk management companies, factoring and financial services, tracking and visibility solutions, compliance and regulatory technology, carrier management systems, and logistics consulting firms","audience_mix":"Freight brokers, 3PL executives, owners and senior managers of logistics companies, operations managers, sales leaders, business development professionals, and decision-makers from third-party logistics providers and transportation intermediaries across North America","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Complete information found. Organized by Transportation Intermediaries Association (TIA) representing the $343 billion 3PL industry. Most attendees are owners and senior managers with buying authority.","original_event_name":"TIA Capital Ideas Conference 2026","original_event_url":"https://web.cvent.com/event/5fcaa2f1-f19b-4e81-a814-d17aa1a29d03/websitePage:fe4fb1cb-f5ba-4897-a32c-606d09490169","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:34:50.627179","master_id":53,"overall_score":6.9,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":10,"rationale":"TIA Capital Ideas Conference explicitly targets third-party logistics providers and freight brokers - exactly the asset-light 3PL and brokerage 3PL segment identified in Criteria Set B as highest-value supply chain vertical. Transportation intermediaries managing logistics operations and dispatch represent core supply chain audience alignment."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":8,"rationale":"Freight brokers, 3PL owners, senior managers, operations managers, and sales leaders all present. These are sales and operations-focused functions aligned with InstaLILY buyer personas. Audience manages high-volume, multi-stakeholder workflows (load matching, carrier assignment, customer management) analogous to distribution sales operations."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":7,"rationale":"April 2026 timing solid. 1,500+ attendees is substantial for vertical-specific event. Phoenix venue accessible. Four-day format with 5+ general sessions and 24+ education tracks indicates meaningful educational programming. TIA organization represents $343 billion industry, indicating established event credibility."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":7,"rationale":"Attendees explicitly include owners and senior managers of logistics companies with buying authority. Most attendees described as owners and senior managers with decision power. Mix of operations managers and sales leaders present. Strong concentration of decision-makers vs. junior staff."}},"reasoning":"TIA Capital Ideas Conference is meaningful opportunity despite outside traditional InstaLILY core verticals. The event targets asset-light 3PLs and freight brokers - exactly the supply chain vertical identified in Criteria Set B as highest alignment. These companies operate high-volume, multi-stakeholder workflows managing load assignment, carrier communication, and customer matching - operationally similar to InstaLILY distribution use cases around order routing and exception handling. However, InstaLILY has not demonstrated explicit freight brokerage or 3PL success stories. Event represents adjacent expansion opportunity rather than core vertical play. April timing and senior manager concentration (owners with buying authority) indicate quality attendees.","sales_brief":"Secondary expansion opportunity - Asset-light 3PLs and freight brokers face similar workflow complexity to InstaLILY distribution customers (high-volume, multi-step, exception-handling). 1,500+ attendees with owner and senior manager concentration = decision-maker density. April timing optimal. TIA represents $343B industry with mature buyer awareness. Risk: Vertical is adjacent to core InstaLILY verticals with no public customer reference. May require education on applicability of distribution-focused InstaWorkers platform to logistics workflows."}'::jsonb
) on conflict (id) do update set
