  'https://www.executiveplatforms.com/names/',
  'executiveplatforms.com/names',
  'April 20, 2026',
  '2026-04-20',
  '2026-04-20',
  'Houston, TX',
  'Hilton Americas-Houston',
  null,
  'A premier gathering of industry leaders, manufacturing executives, and experts dedicated to exploring innovative strategies, emerging trends, and best practices in manufacturing management. Brings together SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Supply Chain, Operations, and Quality, Lean/CI/OpEx Executives, and Plant Managers.',
  'supply_chain_and_distribution',
  'Manufacturing technology providers, workforce management solutions, automation and robotics vendors, continuous improvement consultants, Industry 4.0 solution providers, maintenance and asset management software companies',
  'SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Supply Chain, Operations, and Quality from companies like Toyota, Nestlé Purina, Intel, Estée Lauder, Tesla, 3M, Mattel, Boeing, and Ford. Over 400 attendees with 91% at Director level and above from 200+ global organizations',
  'enriched',
  4.2,
  'While this event has exceptional buyer seniority and scale, it targets manufacturing plants and operations excellence rather than distribution, supply, or field service verticals that align with InstaLILY ICP. Manufacturing plants lack the high-volume sales team execution, multi-location branch operations, and quoting workflows that InstaLILY automates. The vertical mismatch (supply chain alignment score 3) significantly constrains opportunity despite strong executive attendance.',
  'Lower priority. Event attracts C-suite manufacturing executives (strong seniority), but core audience is plant operations and manufacturing excellence rather than distributors or field service companies. InstaLILY solutions target sales execution and multi-location branch operations, not factory floor optimization. Skip unless pursuing manufacturing suppliers or OEM partners specifically.',
  '{"event_name":"North American Manufacturing Excellence Summit (NAMES) 2026","event_url":"https://www.executiveplatforms.com/names/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"April 20, 2026","location":"Houston, TX","cost":null,"venue":"Hilton Americas-Houston","description":"A premier gathering of industry leaders, manufacturing executives, and experts dedicated to exploring innovative strategies, emerging trends, and best practices in manufacturing management. Brings together SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Supply Chain, Operations, and Quality, Lean/CI/OpEx Executives, and Plant Managers.","industry_vertical":"supply_chain_and_distribution","exhibitor_mix":"Manufacturing technology providers, workforce management solutions, automation and robotics vendors, continuous improvement consultants, Industry 4.0 solution providers, maintenance and asset management software companies","audience_mix":"SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Supply Chain, Operations, and Quality from companies like Toyota, Nestlé Purina, Intel, Estée Lauder, Tesla, 3M, Mattel, Boeing, and Ford. Over 400 attendees with 91% at Director level and above from 200+ global organizations","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Event is a single-day summit focused on manufacturing excellence. Cost information not publicly available as this appears to be an invitation-based or executive-level event.","original_event_name":"North American Manufacturing Excellence Summit (NAMES) 2026","original_event_url":"https://www.executiveplatforms.com/names/","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057097","master_id":39,"overall_score":4.2,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":3,"rationale":"Event focuses on manufacturing operations, Lean/CI/OpEx, and continuous improvement rather than distribution, 3PL, brokerage, or procurement functions. Attendees from Toyota, Nestl, Intel, Tesla represent large manufacturers, not distributors or suppliers aligned with InstaLILY ICP. Manufacturing plants are not primary distribution/field service targets."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":7,"rationale":"Strong executive presence with SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Supply Chain, and Operations. These are decision-makers with budget authority. However, manufacturing plant operations differ from distribution sales/operations execution that InstaLILY targets."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":8,"rationale":"Single-day premier event in April 2026, US-based (Houston) and easily accessible to sales team. Established Executive Platforms franchise. 400+ attendees from 200+ organizations indicates solid scale and credibility."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":9,"rationale":"91% of attendees at Director level and above with C-suite representation. High concentration of SVPs and VPs from Fortune 500 manufacturing companies. Strong decision-maker seniority across the board."}},"reasoning":"While this event has exceptional buyer seniority and scale, it targets manufacturing plants and operations excellence rather than distribution, supply, or field service verticals that align with InstaLILY ICP. Manufacturing plants lack the high-volume sales team execution, multi-location branch operations, and quoting workflows that InstaLILY automates. The vertical mismatch (supply chain alignment score 3) significantly constrains opportunity despite strong executive attendance.","sales_brief":"Lower priority. Event attracts C-suite manufacturing executives (strong seniority), but core audience is plant operations and manufacturing excellence rather than distributors or field service companies. InstaLILY solutions target sales execution and multi-location branch operations, not factory floor optimization. Skip unless pursuing manufacturing suppliers or OEM partners specifically."}'::jsonb
) on conflict (id) do update set
