  '2026-05-06',
  'Charlotte, NC',
  'Charlotte Convention Center',
  null,
  'The premier exhibition in the U.S. dedicated to the full supply chain of the fastener industry, bringing together distributors, mechanical and design engineers, purchasers, wholesalers and OEMs. Serves sectors including automotive, aerospace, construction, HVAC, furniture, and appliances.',
  'industrial_parts',
  'Fastener manufacturers (screws, bolts, nuts, washers), raw materials and coatings suppliers (steel, aluminum, brass, titanium, stainless steel), fastening machinery and technology providers, industrial automation and robotics companies, surface treatment and plating technology vendors, assembly and installation systems providers',
  'Distributors, mechanical and design engineers, purchasers, wholesalers, OEMs from automotive, aerospace, construction, HVAC, furniture, and appliance industries. 79% of attendees have final say or influence purchasing decisions, 82% consider the show important to attend',
  'enriched',
  8.9,
  'Fastener Fair USA aligns very strongly with InstaLILY ICP. Fastener distributors are proven high-value targets (Copper State Bolt & Nut reference customer demonstrates success). Multi-location distributors in fastener supply face exact pain points InstaLILY solves: complex SKU management, sales rep quoting efficiency, parts validation across branches. Industry vertical is explicitly industrial_parts. High concentration of distributors and purchasing decision-makers with authority.',
  'High-priority event for InstaLILY. Fastener distributors are proven ICP match (reference customer: Copper State Bolt & Nut). 79% of attendees have purchasing authority, significant distributor and wholesaler concentration. May 2026 timing perfect for H2 sales cycles. Two-day format enables pre-booked meetings strategy. Risk: Highly competitive vendor environment, requires differentiated positioning vs. horizontal ERP/CRM extensions.',
  '{"event_name":"Fastener Fair USA 2026","event_url":"https://www.fastenerfairusa.com/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"May 5-6, 2026","location":"Charlotte, NC","cost":null,"venue":"Charlotte Convention Center","description":"The premier exhibition in the U.S. dedicated to the full supply chain of the fastener industry, bringing together distributors, mechanical and design engineers, purchasers, wholesalers and OEMs. Serves sectors including automotive, aerospace, construction, HVAC, furniture, and appliances.","industry_vertical":"industrial_parts","exhibitor_mix":"Fastener manufacturers (screws, bolts, nuts, washers), raw materials and coatings suppliers (steel, aluminum, brass, titanium, stainless steel), fastening machinery and technology providers, industrial automation and robotics companies, surface treatment and plating technology vendors, assembly and installation systems providers","audience_mix":"Distributors, mechanical and design engineers, purchasers, wholesalers, OEMs from automotive, aerospace, construction, HVAC, furniture, and appliance industries. 79% of attendees have final say or influence purchasing decisions, 82% consider the show important to attend","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Event co-located with ALUMINUM Fabrication Summit. Attendee registration cost not specified on public website.","original_event_name":"Fastener Fair USA","original_event_url":"https://www.fastenerfairusa.com/","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057130","master_id":41,"overall_score":8.9,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":9,"rationale":"Strong alignment with InstaLILY target functions. Audience explicitly includes distributors, purchasers, and wholesalers - core sales and procurement decision-makers. OEMs and design engineers also present but secondary to distribution buyer focus. 79% of attendees have final say or influence on purchasing decisions, indicating high buyer authority."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":8,"rationale":"Two-day event in May 2026, well-established trade show for fastener industry. Charlotte, NC location is US-accessible and convenient for sales team deployment. 2-day format is optimal for meaningful engagement and pre-booked meeting strategy."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":9,"rationale":"Attendee base skews toward decision-makers and procurement authority (79% with purchasing influence). While specific C-suite percentages not detailed, the purchasing influence metric and distributor/wholesaler focus indicates high-level buyer presence. Likely mix of directors, branch managers, and procurement VPs."}},"reasoning":"Fastener Fair USA aligns very strongly with InstaLILY ICP. Fastener distributors are proven high-value targets (Copper State Bolt & Nut reference customer demonstrates success). Multi-location distributors in fastener supply face exact pain points InstaLILY solves: complex SKU management, sales rep quoting efficiency, parts validation across branches. Industry vertical is explicitly industrial_parts. High concentration of distributors and purchasing decision-makers with authority.","sales_brief":"High-priority event for InstaLILY. Fastener distributors are proven ICP match (reference customer: Copper State Bolt & Nut). 79% of attendees have purchasing authority, significant distributor and wholesaler concentration. May 2026 timing perfect for H2 sales cycles. Two-day format enables pre-booked meetings strategy. Risk: Highly competitive vendor environment, requires differentiated positioning vs. horizontal ERP/CRM extensions."}'::jsonb
) on conflict (id) do update set
