  'Moderate fit. Healthcare/pharma is InstaLILY vertical, but CPHI Americas targets drug manufacturers and CDMOs rather than medical/pharmaceutical distributors. Event focuses on contract manufacturing ecosystem and technical operations, not sales execution or multi-location field distribution. Consider only if pursuing CDMO operations optimization angles; higher-value focus should be distribution-specific pharma trade shows.',
  '{"event_name":"CPHI Americas 2026","event_url":"https://www.cphi.com/americas/en/home.html","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"June 2-4, 2026","location":"Philadelphia, PA","cost":null,"venue":"Pennsylvania Convention Center","description":"A premium, content-first pharmaceutical industry event specifically centered around the contract development and manufacturing (CDMO/CMO) ecosystem. Brings together the complete pharmaceutical supply chain with a focus on strategic partnerships and business development.","industry_vertical":"pharmaceuticals","exhibitor_mix":"Contract development and manufacturing organizations (CDMOs/CMOs), API and excipient suppliers, pharmaceutical equipment and technology providers, biopharmaceutical companies, packaging and drug delivery innovators, analytical chemistry service providers, containment and isolation technology vendors","audience_mix":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing executives, R&D leaders, procurement managers, supply chain directors, regulatory experts, quality professionals, business development executives from drug manufacturers, biotech companies, and pharmaceutical service providers. Expected 2,735+ attendees with decision-making authority","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Reimagined format for 2026 with enhanced focus on contract manufacturing ecosystem. Formerly known as CPHI North America.","original_event_name":"CPHI Americas 2026","original_event_url":"https://www.cphi.com/americas/en/home.html","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057132","master_id":43,"overall_score":5.1,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":6,"rationale":"Mixed functional alignment. Audience includes procurement managers, supply chain directors, and manufacturing executives who align with InstaLILY operations targets. However, R&D leaders, regulatory experts, quality professionals, and business development executives represent adjacent/supporting functions rather than core sales or operations execution roles. CDMO/CMO focus is manufacturing-centric rather than distribution or field service."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":8,"rationale":"Major 3-day event in June 2026, Philadelphia location is US-accessible. Expected 2,735+ attendees indicates strong scale. Established CPHI brand with renamed/reimagined 2026 format. Well-timed within H1/early H2 sales cycles."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":7,"rationale":"Attendee base includes manufacturing executives, procurement managers, and supply chain directors with decision-making authority. However, audience is more diverse across technical, regulatory, and R&D functions rather than concentrated in high-level executive procurement/operations roles. Mix of mid-level and senior attendees."}},"reasoning":"Partial alignment with healthcare/pharma vertical (one of five InstaLILY ICP verticals), but event focuses on CDMO/CMO manufacturing partnerships and pharmaceutical supply chain rather than distributors of medical supplies or pharmaceutical products. The audience skews toward manufacturing operations, R&D, and regulatory - not sales execution or high-volume distributor workflows. InstaLILY would target pharmaceutical/medical distributors, not drug manufacturers or CDMOs. Vertical match is weak.","sales_brief":"Moderate fit. Healthcare/pharma is InstaLILY vertical, but CPHI Americas targets drug manufacturers and CDMOs rather than medical/pharmaceutical distributors. Event focuses on contract manufacturing ecosystem and technical operations, not sales execution or multi-location field distribution. Consider only if pursuing CDMO operations optimization angles; higher-value focus should be distribution-specific pharma trade shows."}'::jsonb
