  'Low priority - Not InstaLILY ICP alignment despite pharma industry presence. Event audience is process engineers, plant managers, and equipment vendors focused on manufacturing operations and production optimization, not the distributor/supplier/field-service buyer personas InstaLILY targets. No material presence of sales operations, inventory management, or multi-location supply chain attendees. Recommend passing unless pharmaceutical distribution companies are confirmed as exhibitors or major attendee sponsors. Risk: Brand new event with uncertain attendance quality and buyer composition - insufficient data to justify resource allocation.',
  '{"event_name":"ChemE Show – Powered by ACHEMA 2026","event_url":"https://www.achema.de/en/the-achema/cheme-show/short-profile","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"June 9-10, 2026","location":"Houston, TX","cost":null,"venue":"George R. Brown Convention Center","description":"A groundbreaking new annual event for experts, decision-makers and solution providers along the chemical and bio-based production value chain. Highlights cutting-edge advancements in process engineering, biotechnology, and downstream processing, while bridging connections to the energy industry.","industry_vertical":"others","exhibitor_mix":"Chemical engineering equipment providers, process automation and control systems vendors, biotechnology solution providers, pharmaceutical manufacturing technology companies, heat exchangers and separation systems manufacturers, pumps and valves suppliers, hydrogen and clean energy technology providers, laboratory equipment and analytics companies","audience_mix":"Chemical engineers, CTOs, process and project engineers, plant managers, EPC firms, technology licensors, biopharma executives, CMOs, facility planners, regulatory professionals, QC leads from chemical, pharmaceutical, and energy industries","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Brand new event launching in 2026 as a partnership between Gulf Energy Information and DECHEMA (organizers of ACHEMA). Will feature standalone U.S. events in 2026 and 2028.","original_event_name":"ChemE Show – Powered by ACHEMA","original_event_url":"https://www.achema.de/en/the-achema/cheme-show/short-profile","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057135","master_id":45,"overall_score":2.1,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":2,"rationale":"ChemE Show is focused on chemical engineering, process automation, and biotechnology manufacturing - not distribution, supply chain operations, or field service delivery. While pharma is in InstaLILY ICP, this event targets equipment providers, engineers, and manufacturing plant operations rather than distributors, suppliers, or field-service organizations. No alignment with InstaLILY vertical-specific distribution or supply-chain operating models."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":3,"rationale":"Audience is primarily chemical engineers, CTOs, plant managers, process engineers, and regulatory professionals - technical and manufacturing-focused roles. These are not sales, operations, or distribution functions that InstaLILY targets. Decision-makers here own manufacturing workflows, not the repetitive quoting, order entry, or inventory management workflows that AI Teammates automate."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":6,"rationale":"New event launching in 2026 at major Houston venue (George R. Brown) suggests significant backing and potential for strong attendance. US-based and well-timed for 2026 calendar. However, brand new event means uncertain attendance quality, no historical data on buyer concentration, and potentially unproven draw for targeted buyer personas."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":2,"rationale":"Heavy presence of technical specialists (chemical engineers, process engineers, QC leads, facility planners) rather than business decision-makers. CTOs and plant managers are senior but own manufacturing operations, not commercial distribution or sales operations where InstaLILY creates value. Limited executive presence for commercial technology purchasing."}},"reasoning":"ChemE Show falls outside InstaLILY ICP despite pharma industry overlap. The event is engineered for process engineers, equipment manufacturers, and plant operations professionals focused on chemical manufacturing workflows and upstream/downstream processing optimization. InstaLILY targets distributors, suppliers, and field-service organizations that handle order management, parts logistics, and sales velocity - functions not present at a manufacturing/engineering-focused event. While healthcare/pharma is in InstaLILY vertical list, this event serves manufacturing operations (pharma CMOs, plant managers) not pharmaceutical supply chain, medical device distribution, or healthcare supply distribution where InstaLILY creates measurable ROI. New event status adds execution risk.","sales_brief":"Low priority - Not InstaLILY ICP alignment despite pharma industry presence. Event audience is process engineers, plant managers, and equipment vendors focused on manufacturing operations and production optimization, not the distributor/supplier/field-service buyer personas InstaLILY targets. No material presence of sales operations, inventory management, or multi-location supply chain attendees. Recommend passing unless pharmaceutical distribution companies are confirmed as exhibitors or major attendee sponsors. Risk: Brand new event with uncertain attendance quality and buyer composition - insufficient data to justify resource allocation."}'::jsonb
