  'San Diego Convention Center',
  'Registration varies by type - Premier Access includes BIO Partnering and ranges from member to non-member rates. Save up to $700 as BIO member',
  'The world''s largest biotechnology event bringing together leaders from biopharma, biotech, academia and investment. Features 130+ sessions in 18 focus areas including AI & digital health, cell and gene therapy, oncology, business development, and next-generation biotherapeutics. Includes proprietary BIO Partnering platform for structured business meetings.',
  'pharmaceuticals',
  'Biotechnology and biopharmaceutical companies, research institutions, contract research and manufacturing organizations (CROs/CDMOs), life sciences technology providers, diagnostic companies, investment firms, pharmaceutical service providers, laboratory equipment and reagent suppliers',
  'Over 16,000 attendees from 65+ countries including C-suite executives, research directors, investors, regulatory professionals, scientists, business development leaders from pharmaceutical companies, biotech startups, academia, and government agencies. 1,600+ exhibitors representing innovative startups and global industry leaders',
  'enriched',
  3.8,
  'While BIO Convention is massive and prestigious, it targets biotech/biopharmaceutical companies at research, development, and investment stages rather than pharmaceutical/medical distributors or healthcare field service operations. InstaLILY targets healthcare/pharma distributors (medical supplies, pharmaceuticals), not drug manufacturers or biotech startups. Event focuses on drug discovery, cell therapy, and investment partnerships rather than supply chain operations or sales execution workflows.',
  'Low priority despite scale and prestige. BIO targets biotech/biopharma innovators and investors, not medical distributors or healthcare field service companies. InstaLILY vertical is healthcare distributors (medical supplies, pharma products), not drug manufacturers. 16,000+ attendees mostly researchers, scientists, and venture investors rather than operations/sales executives. High noise-to-signal ratio. Skip unless specifically targeting biotech supply chain partnerships.',
  '{"event_name":"BIO International Convention 2026","event_url":"https://convention.bio.org/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"June 22-25, 2026","location":"San Diego, CA","cost":"Registration varies by type - Premier Access includes BIO Partnering and ranges from member to non-member rates. Save up to $700 as BIO member","venue":"San Diego Convention Center","description":"The world''s largest biotechnology event bringing together leaders from biopharma, biotech, academia and investment. Features 130+ sessions in 18 focus areas including AI & digital health, cell and gene therapy, oncology, business development, and next-generation biotherapeutics. Includes proprietary BIO Partnering platform for structured business meetings.","industry_vertical":"pharmaceuticals","exhibitor_mix":"Biotechnology and biopharmaceutical companies, research institutions, contract research and manufacturing organizations (CROs/CDMOs), life sciences technology providers, diagnostic companies, investment firms, pharmaceutical service providers, laboratory equipment and reagent suppliers","audience_mix":"Over 16,000 attendees from 65+ countries including C-suite executives, research directors, investors, regulatory professionals, scientists, business development leaders from pharmaceutical companies, biotech startups, academia, and government agencies. 1,600+ exhibitors representing innovative startups and global industry leaders","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Largest global biotech event with extensive partnering component. 2025 edition (Boston) had 20,559+ companies from 73 countries with 57,044 partnering meetings. Company presentation fee: $2,000 members / $2,475 non-members.","original_event_name":"BIO International Convention 2026","original_event_url":"https://convention.bio.org/","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057136","master_id":47,"overall_score":3.8,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":5,"rationale":"Diverse attendee base including C-suite executives, research directors, investors, scientists, business development leaders, and regulatory professionals. While some sales/BD functions present, primary focus is research, investment, and biotechnology advancement rather than sales execution or operations optimization. Investor and academic presence dilutes practical buyer concentration."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":9,"rationale":"World''s largest biotech event with 16,000+ attendees from 65+ countries and 1,600+ exhibitors. June 2026 timing is US-accessible (San Diego). Established flagship event with proven scale, credibility, and networking value. Attendance numbers are exceptional and demonstrate major industry influence."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":8,"rationale":"High concentration of C-suite executives, research directors, and investors. Large biotech companies and startups represented. Decision-maker seniority is strong. However, scientific researcher and investor presence limits operational buyer focus compared to manufacturing/distribution executives."}},"reasoning":"While BIO Convention is massive and prestigious, it targets biotech/biopharmaceutical companies at research, development, and investment stages rather than pharmaceutical/medical distributors or healthcare field service operations. InstaLILY targets healthcare/pharma distributors (medical supplies, pharmaceuticals), not drug manufacturers or biotech startups. Event focuses on drug discovery, cell therapy, and investment partnerships rather than supply chain operations or sales execution workflows.","sales_brief":"Low priority despite scale and prestige. BIO targets biotech/biopharma innovators and investors, not medical distributors or healthcare field service companies. InstaLILY vertical is healthcare distributors (medical supplies, pharma products), not drug manufacturers. 16,000+ attendees mostly researchers, scientists, and venture investors rather than operations/sales executives. High noise-to-signal ratio. Skip unless specifically targeting biotech supply chain partnerships."}'::jsonb
