  4.1,
  'Event targets pharmaceutical manufacturing executives and plant operations excellence rather than pharmaceutical or medical distributors. InstaLILY healthcare/pharma ICP focus is on distributors of medical supplies and pharmaceutical products - not drug manufacturers or pharmaceutical plant operations. Manufacturing plant operations differ fundamentally from multi-location distributor sales execution and field service workflows that InstaLILY automates. Vertical mismatch despite strong buyer seniority.',
  'Lower priority. PMWS attracts C-suite pharmaceutical manufacturing executives (strong seniority), but targets plant operations and technical manufacturing excellence. InstaLILY healthcare vertical is medical/pharmaceutical distributors, not drug manufacturers. No alignment with sales execution, multi-location branch operations, or field service workflows. Consider only if pursuing pharmaceutical supplier partnerships; focus sales resources on medical/pharma distribution trade shows instead.',
  '{"event_name":"Pharma Manufacturing World Summit (PMWS) 2026","event_url":"https://www.executiveplatforms.com/pmws/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"May 18-20, 2026","location":"Boston, MA","cost":null,"venue":"Boston Marriott Copley Place","description":"A premier gathering of pharmaceutical industry leaders, manufacturing executives, and experts dedicated to exploring innovative strategies, emerging trends, and best practices in pharmaceutical management. Brings together senior executives focused on manufacturing excellence, quality, and supply chain optimization.","industry_vertical":"pharmaceuticals","exhibitor_mix":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing technology providers, quality management systems vendors, automation and digital transformation solutions, supply chain optimization platforms, technical operations consultants, maintenance and reliability technology companies, pharmaceutical equipment manufacturers","audience_mix":"SVPs, VPs, and Directors of Manufacturing, Technical Operations, Quality, and Supply Chain from major pharmaceutical and biopharmaceutical companies including Eli Lilly, Takeda, Bristol Myers Squibb, Halozyme, and other global pharma organizations. Approximately 200 attendees primarily at Director level and above, including Technology Leaders and Plant/Site/Facility Managers","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Three-day summit with approximately 30 exhibitors and 52 speakers. Organized by Executive Platforms (same organizer as NAMES). Focused on pharmaceutical manufacturing operations and excellence.","original_event_name":"Pharma Manufacturing World Summit 2026","original_event_url":"https://www.executiveplatforms.com/pmws/","added_to_master":"2026-04-07T12:55:39.057138","master_id":49,"overall_score":4.1,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":7,"rationale":"Strong executive presence in manufacturing, technical operations, quality, and supply chain optimization. SVPs, VPs, and Directors represent operations and quality decision-makers. However, audience focuses on pharmaceutical manufacturing operations and plant optimization rather than sales execution or multi-location field distribution/service operations InstaLILY targets."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":7,"rationale":"Three-day event in May 2026, Boston location is US-accessible and convenient. Approximately 200 attendees from global pharma organizations indicates solid but smaller-scale event compared to major trade shows. 30 exhibitors and 52 speakers suggest professional, curated summit format rather than massive trade show."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":9,"rationale":"Attendees primarily at Director level and above, including SVPs, VPs, and Technology Leaders from major pharmaceutical companies (Eli Lilly, Takeda, Bristol Myers Squibb, etc.). High concentration of C-suite and senior executive decision-makers with significant budget authority."}},"reasoning":"Event targets pharmaceutical manufacturing executives and plant operations excellence rather than pharmaceutical or medical distributors. InstaLILY healthcare/pharma ICP focus is on distributors of medical supplies and pharmaceutical products - not drug manufacturers or pharmaceutical plant operations. Manufacturing plant operations differ fundamentally from multi-location distributor sales execution and field service workflows that InstaLILY automates. Vertical mismatch despite strong buyer seniority.","sales_brief":"Lower priority. PMWS attracts C-suite pharmaceutical manufacturing executives (strong seniority), but targets plant operations and technical manufacturing excellence. InstaLILY healthcare vertical is medical/pharmaceutical distributors, not drug manufacturers. No alignment with sales execution, multi-location branch operations, or field service workflows. Consider only if pursuing pharmaceutical supplier partnerships; focus sales resources on medical/pharma distribution trade shows instead."}'::jsonb
