  '22173552-a4c5-5b92-be82-8f992c9e5bb1',
  'IEEE PES T&D 2026 - Transmission & Distribution Conference & Exposition',
  'https://ieeet-d.org/',
  'ieeet-d.org',
  'May 4-7, 2026',
  '2026-05-04',
  '2026-05-07',
  'Chicago, Illinois',
  'McCormick Place - South Building',
  'Varies by package - early bird pricing available through April 2026; utility saver packages available for groups of 5 or 10',
  'North America''s leading Transmission & Distribution Conference and Exposition for power and energy professionals. A biennial event featuring technical sessions, world-class exhibition, and networking opportunities focused on the design, operation, and modernization of the electric grid.',
  'others',
  'Over 800 exhibiting companies including utilities, technology developers, equipment manufacturers, solution providers, and vendors offering transmission and distribution products, services, and innovations for the electric power industry',
  'Power and energy professionals including utility executives and engineers, grid operators, power systems and electrical engineers, policymakers and regulators, researchers and academic professionals, consultants, IT providers, and students/young professionals in the power and energy field',
  'enriched',
  1.8,
  'IEEE PES T&D 2026 is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY ICP. The event serves the electric utility and power transmission/distribution infrastructure sector - a completely different industry vertical from InstaLILY target markets (construction supply, industrial parts, healthcare, automotive goods, food supply distributors). Attendees are power systems engineers, grid operators, and utility operations professionals managing electrical infrastructure, not commercial distributors managing inventory, quoting, or field service execution. The buying personas and use cases are entirely orthogonal to InstaLILY problem set. While the event is large and prestigious, it represents zero strategic fit for lead generation.',
  'Skip this event. IEEE PES T&D targets utility/power infrastructure sector with engineering and grid operations buyers - completely outside InstaLILY ICP of commercial distributors and field service companies. No sales, quoting, inventory, or order management buyers present. Investment would yield zero qualified leads.',
  '{"event_name":"IEEE PES T&D 2026 - Transmission & Distribution Conference & Exposition","event_url":"https://ieeet-d.org/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"May 4-7, 2026","location":"Chicago, Illinois","cost":"Varies by package - early bird pricing available through April 2026; utility saver packages available for groups of 5 or 10","venue":"McCormick Place - South Building","description":"North America''s leading Transmission & Distribution Conference and Exposition for power and energy professionals. A biennial event featuring technical sessions, world-class exhibition, and networking opportunities focused on the design, operation, and modernization of the electric grid.","industry_vertical":"others","exhibitor_mix":"Over 800 exhibiting companies including utilities, technology developers, equipment manufacturers, solution providers, and vendors offering transmission and distribution products, services, and innovations for the electric power industry","audience_mix":"Power and energy professionals including utility executives and engineers, grid operators, power systems and electrical engineers, policymakers and regulators, researchers and academic professionals, consultants, IT providers, and students/young professionals in the power and energy field","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Specific pricing amounts not publicly displayed on website; requires accessing registration portal. Event is held every two years and is recognized as the most prominent T&D conference in North America with expected attendance of 15,000+ professionals.","original_event_name":"IEEE","original_event_url":"https://ieeet-d.org/","added_to_master":"2026-04-21T20:03:05.714288","master_id":43,"overall_score":1.8,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":2,"rationale":"Attendee base is primarily power systems engineers, grid operators, electrical engineers, and utility operations teams. While operations-focused, these are infrastructure/engineering operations roles, not commercial distribution or sales operations that drive InstaLILY value. No sales enablement, quoting, order management, or field service execution functions represented. Audience skews heavily technical and regulatory rather than business operations."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":3,"rationale":"Event is large and well-established (15,000+ attendees, 900+ exhibitors, biennial major conference) occurring in May 2026 within proper timeframe. However, geography and format are challenging for InstaLILY sales team resource allocation. Highly technical, engineering-focused conference format makes traditional enterprise sales outreach difficult."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":2,"rationale":"Mix includes utility executives and decision-makers, but majority of attendees are engineers, technicians, system planners, and operational staff rather than C-suite or VP-level buyers with budget authority for enterprise software platforms. Decision-makers present are focused on infrastructure and grid modernization, not business process automation or sales/operations technology."}},"reasoning":"IEEE PES T&D 2026 is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY ICP. The event serves the electric utility and power transmission/distribution infrastructure sector - a completely different industry vertical from InstaLILY target markets (construction supply, industrial parts, healthcare, automotive goods, food supply distributors). Attendees are power systems engineers, grid operators, and utility operations professionals managing electrical infrastructure, not commercial distributors managing inventory, quoting, or field service execution. The buying personas and use cases are entirely orthogonal to InstaLILY problem set. While the event is large and prestigious, it represents zero strategic fit for lead generation.","sales_brief":"Skip this event. IEEE PES T&D targets utility/power infrastructure sector with engineering and grid operations buyers - completely