  'Jacob K. Javits Convention Center',
  'All-Access Pass: $900 (NRF Members) / $1,500 (Non-Members); Retail Expo Pass: $100',
  'The world''s leading retail exhibition and conference bringing together global retailers, technology innovators, and industry leaders to explore trends, technologies, and ideas shaping the future of commerce. Features 1,000+ exhibitors, 175+ sessions, and networking opportunities across three days.',
  'others',
  'Retail technology providers, AI and automation innovators, POS systems, supply chain and logistics platforms, ecommerce solutions, payment platforms, inventory management systems, customer experience tools, RFID technology, robotics companies, WMS providers, data analytics firms, omnichannel retail solutions, startup companies in retail tech innovation',
  'Senior retail executives (CEOs, C-suite leaders), merchandising leaders, digital transformation heads, IT directors, supply chain managers, store operations professionals, marketing strategists, warehouse operators, digital commerce managers, solution buyers from retailers and brands across apparel, food service, home goods, specialty retail, and various retail segments from 100+ countries',
  'enriched',
  2.1,
  'NRF 2026 is a world-class event with exceptional scale, timing, and executive seniority - but it is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY''s ICP. The event serves retail merchants (Target, Walmart, etc.) and retail technology vendors, not B2B distributors or field-service organizations. InstaLILY''s AI Teammates solve problems for wholesale distributors managing complex parts catalogs and multi-location sales operations - not retail store operations, merchandising, or consumer supply chains. While some supply chain professionals attend, they are retail supply chain focused, not distribution-facing. Attending would mean competing for retail CIOs attention when InstaLILY has no product-market fit with retail merchants. Better ROI exists in vertical-specific distribution events.',
  'Skip this event. NRF targets retail merchants and retail tech vendors, not B2B distributors or suppliers. InstaLILY solves wholesale distribution problems (parts quoting, multi-location sales ops, tribal knowledge), not retail store operations or consumer supply chains. Attending would waste resources on wrong buyer personas. Focus on HARDI, AED Summit, and automotive/industrial parts distribution events instead.',
  '{"event_name":"NRF 2026: Retail''s Big Show","event_url":"https://nrfbigshow.nrf.com/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"January 11-13, 2026","location":"New York City, NY","cost":"All-Access Pass: $900 (NRF Members) / $1,500 (Non-Members); Retail Expo Pass: $100","venue":"Jacob K. Javits Convention Center","description":"The world''s leading retail exhibition and conference bringing together global retailers, technology innovators, and industry leaders to explore trends, technologies, and ideas shaping the future of commerce. Features 1,000+ exhibitors, 175+ sessions, and networking opportunities across three days.","industry_vertical":"others","exhibitor_mix":"Retail technology providers, AI and automation innovators, POS systems, supply chain and logistics platforms, ecommerce solutions, payment platforms, inventory management systems, customer experience tools, RFID technology, robotics companies, WMS providers, data analytics firms, omnichannel retail solutions, startup companies in retail tech innovation","audience_mix":"Senior retail executives (CEOs, C-suite leaders), merchandising leaders, digital transformation heads, IT directors, supply chain managers, store operations professionals, marketing strategists, warehouse operators, digital commerce managers, solution buyers from retailers and brands across apparel, food service, home goods, specialty retail, and various retail segments from 100+ countries","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Comprehensive information found including dates, venue, pricing, attendee demographics, and exhibitor types. Event had 40,000 attendees in 2025 with representation from 98+ countries. Theme for 2026 is ''The Next Now'' focusing on AI, automation, and retail transformation.","original_event_name":"National Retail Federation","original_event_url":"https://nrfbigshow.nrf.com/","added_to_master":"2026-04-23T18:23:26.941372","master_id":44,"overall_score":2.1,"scores":{"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":3,"rationale":"While the event attracts senior retail executives and supply chain managers, the primary audience is retail merchants, digital commerce leaders, and merchandising teams. InstaLILY targets distributors, suppliers, and field-service operations - not retail end-buyers. Supply chain managers present are typically focused on inbound fulfillment and retail logistics rather than B2B distribution operations, quoting systems, or parts catalogs that drive InstaLILY value."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":9,"rationale":"Major annual US event in January 2026 with 40,000+ attendees, established 30+ year reputation, and premium venue (Javits Center NYC). Easily accessible to US sales team and represents one of retail industrys largest gatherings. Timing is optimal for Q1 2026 outreach campaigns."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":8,"rationale":"High concentration of C-suite executives (CEOs, Chief Digital Officers, VP Supply Chain) with significant budget authority attending. Strong presence of senior decision-makers from major national and international retailers. Speaker lineup likely includes retail industry leaders with enterprise purchasing power."}},"reasoning":"NRF 2026 is a world-class event with exceptional scale, timing, and executive seniority - but it is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY''s ICP. The event serves retail merchants (Target, Walmart, etc.) and retail technology vendors, not B2B distributors or field-service organizations. InstaLILY''s AI Teammates solve problems for wholesale distributors managing complex parts catalogs and multi-location sales operations - not retail store operations, merchandising, or consumer supply chains. While some supply chain professionals attend, they are retail supply chain focused, not distribution-facing. Attending would mean competing for retail CIOs attention when InstaLILY has no product-market fit with retail merchants. Better ROI exists in vertical-specific distribution events.","sales_brief":"Skip this event. NRF targets retail merchants and retail tech vendors, not B2B distributors or suppliers. InstaLILY solves wholesale distribution problems (parts quoting, multi-location sales ops, tribal knowledge), not retail store operations or consumer supply chains. Attending would waste resources on wrong buyer personas. Focus on HARDI, AED Summit, and automotive/industrial parts distribution events instead."}'::jsonb
