  'November 9-11, 2026',
  '2026-11-09',
  '2026-11-11',
  'Atlanta, GA',
  'Grand Hyatt Atlanta in Buckhead',
  null,
  'B2B Online Atlanta is a premier three-day conference focused on B2B eCommerce, digital marketing, and sales transformation for manufacturers and distributors. The event brings together senior-level professionals to explore topics including omnichannel strategy, AI, SEO, customer experience, and digital innovation through keynotes, workshops, interactive panels, and networking sessions.',
  'supply_chain_and_distribution',
  'eCommerce technology providers, digital marketing platforms, AI and personalization solutions, customer experience tools, commerce platforms (including companies like commercetools, Hygraph, inriver PIM), MarTech and AdTech vendors, and B2B-specific software solutions focused on helping manufacturers and distributors with digital transformation',
  'Senior executives from manufacturing and distribution companies including CMOs, VPs of eCommerce, Directors of Digital Marketing, IT Directors, Customer Experience leaders, Digital Transformation officers, and eCommerce managers. Expected attendance of 300-600+ professionals primarily from enterprise and mid-market B2B organizations across North America focused on digital commerce strategy and implementation',
  'enriched',
  5.8,
  'B2B Online Atlanta 2026 is a well-timed, senior-executive-rich event in a target geography. However, it is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY go-to-market strategy. The conference is designed for B2B eCommerce and digital marketing transformation - customer-facing, front-office digital strategy. InstaLILY solves back-office operational problems: quoting automation, parts validation, sales rep workflow efficiency, tribal knowledge codification, high-volume claim processing. The attendee base (CMOs, eCommerce VPs, MarTech buyers) does not match InstaLILY buyer personas. While some attendees work at distributors in target verticals, they are not seeking AI Teammates for operational execution - they are seeking digital commerce, personalization, and marketing tools. Spending resources here would result in cold meetings with wrong functional buyers. Much better ROI exists at industry-specific distribution conferences (HARDI, NAFA, healthcare supply chain events) where operations, procurement, and sales execution leaders gather.',
  'PASS - Wrong buyer functions despite right company types. Event is eCommerce and MarTech focused; attendees (CMOs, eCommerce VPs) are not InstaLILY buyers. We need operations, sales, and supply chain leaders who own execution workflows and face tribal knowledge/manual process pain. Better ROI at vertical-specific distribution conferences targeting procurement, operations, and field service functions.',
  '{"event_name":"B2B Online Atlanta 2026","event_url":"https://b2bmarketingeast.wbresearch.com/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"November 9-11, 2026","location":"Atlanta, GA","cost":null,"venue":"Grand Hyatt Atlanta in Buckhead","description":"B2B Online Atlanta is a premier three-day conference focused on B2B eCommerce, digital marketing, and sales transformation for manufacturers and distributors. The event brings together senior-level professionals to explore topics including omnichannel strategy, AI, SEO, customer experience, and digital innovation through keynotes, workshops, interactive panels, and networking sessions.","industry_vertical":"supply_chain_and_distribution","exhibitor_mix":"eCommerce technology providers, digital marketing platforms, AI and personalization solutions, customer experience tools, commerce platforms (including companies like commercetools, Hygraph, inriver PIM), MarTech and AdTech vendors, and B2B-specific software solutions focused on helping manufacturers and distributors with digital transformation","audience_mix":"Senior executives from manufacturing and distribution companies including CMOs, VPs of eCommerce, Directors of Digital Marketing, IT Directors, Customer Experience leaders, Digital Transformation officers, and eCommerce managers. Expected attendance of 300-600+ professionals primarily from enterprise and mid-market B2B organizations across North America focused on digital commerce strategy and implementation","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"All key information successfully found. Event registration/ticket pricing not publicly available on website (appears to require inquiry). The 2026 event dates and venue are confirmed. Hotel rate for attendees is $259 + $5 GA state fee + tax at Grand Hyatt Atlanta.","original_event_name":"B2B Online Atlanta","original_event_url":"https://b2bmarketingeast.wbresearch.com/","added_to_master":"2026-04-23T22:27:50.634050","master_id":45,"overall_score":5.8,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":4,"rationale":"Event targets manufacturers and distributors broadly, which includes InstaLILY ICP verticals. However, the primary focus is eCommerce, digital marketing, and customer experience transformation rather than operational execution, workflow automation, or supply chain execution. While distributors attend, the conference is not designed for supply chain operations, procurement optimization, or field service execution - the core use cases where InstaLILY drives measurable ROI. Vertical alignment exists but is indirect."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":6,"rationale":"Attendee mix heavily skews toward marketing and digital commerce functions - CMOs, VPs of eCommerce, Digital Marketing Directors. While some operational roles present (IT Directors, Digital Transformation officers), the event is primarily designed for customer-facing digital strategy rather than back-office operations, sales execution, or field service management where InstaLILY creates impact. Functional mismatch with InstaLILY buyer personas who need workflow automation and operational AI."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":8,"rationale":"Established annual B2B conference in major US city (Atlanta) with 300-600+ expected attendees. November 2026 timing is within target window and accessible to US sales team. Three-day format allows meaningful engagement. Solid event scale and logistics, though not mega-conference tier."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":7,"rationale":"Strong concentration of senior executives - CMOs, VPs, Directors from enterprise and mid-market organizations. Clear presence of decision-makers with budget authority for digital transformation initiatives. However, seniority is concentrated in marketing and eCommerce leadership rather than operations, supply chain, or sales execution leadership where InstaLILY deals close."}},"reasoning":"B2B Online Atlanta 2026 is a well-timed, senior-executive-rich event in a target geography. However, it is fundamentally misaligned with InstaLILY go-to-market strategy. The conference is designed for B2B eCommerce and digital marketing transformation - customer-facing, front-office digital strategy. InstaLILY solves back-office operational problems: quoting automation, parts validation, sales rep workflow efficiency, tribal knowledge codification, high-volume claim processing. The attendee base (CMOs, eCommerce VPs, MarTech buyers) does not match InstaLILY buyer personas. While some attendees work at distributors in target verticals, they are not seeking AI Teammates for operational execution - they are seeking digital commerce, personalization, and marketing tools. Spending resources here would result in cold meetings with wrong functional buyers. Much better ROI exists at industry-specific distribution conferences (HARDI, NAFA, healthcare supply chain events) where operations, procurement, and sales execution leaders gather.","sales_brief":"PASS - Wrong buyer functions despite right company types. Event is eCommerce and MarTech focused; attendees (CMOs, eCommerce VPs) are not InstaLILY buyers. We need operations, sales, and supply chain leaders who own execution workflows and face tribal knowledge/manual process pain. Better ROI at vertical-specific distribution conferences targeting procurement, operations, and field service functions."}'::jsonb
