  'Exhibition free to attend; booth costs typically $15k-$40k',
  'Home Delivery World USA 2026 is a premier conference and exhibition focused on retail logistics, e-commerce fulfillment, and last-mile delivery. Co-located with The Middle Mile, this 14-year running event covers the entire supply chain journey from warehouse to final customer delivery, including drayage, warehousing, inventory management, fulfillment, routing, dispatch, last-mile delivery, and returns.',
  'supply_chain_and_distribution',
  'Logistics providers (AIT Worldwide Logistics, Penske, J.B. Hunt, OneRail), technology companies (warehouse automation, robotics, AI-powered logistics, route optimization software, tracking systems), delivery service providers (last-mile carriers, autonomous delivery vehicles, electric fleet vehicles, drone technology), 3PLs, packaging solutions providers, freight management platforms, and e-commerce logistics technology vendors. Over 300+ exhibitors from across the e-commerce and logistics spectrum.',
  'Professionals from e-commerce, retail logistics, and supply chain sectors including retailers (Target, Wayfair, Williams-Sonoma, 7-Eleven, Kroger, IKEA), manufacturers, grocers, logistics managers, supply chain directors, distribution center operators, technology providers, delivery service managers, and transportation professionals. Typically draws 2,000-5,000 attendees with 250+ expert speakers.',
  'enriched',
  4.1,
  'Home Delivery World USA is a large, well-established supply chain event with strong execution in the last-mile logistics and e-commerce fulfillment space. However, it represents poor strategic fit for InstaLILY. The event serves asset-light 3PLs, freight forwarders, last-mile carriers, and e-commerce retailers - none of which are InstaLILY target verticals. InstaLILY solves for B2B distributors (construction, industrial parts, healthcare, automotive, food supply) and field service operations that need sales enablement, quoting automation, parts validation, and exception handling. Home Delivery World attendees operate in fundamentally different business models with different pain points (fulfillment speed, delivery optimization, warehouse robotics) rather than sales velocity, tribal knowledge, or multi-location branch management. While some supply chain functions overlap, the vertical misalignment and buyer functional mismatch make this a low-priority event for resource investment.',
  'Low priority event for InstaLILY. While scale and timing are strong, vertical misalignment is critical - event serves e-commerce/3PL/last-mile logistics, not B2B distributors or field service operations. Attendees optimize for fulfillment and delivery, not sales enablement or quoting. Risk of wasted booth spend and poor lead quality. Better resource allocation exists in verticals like HARDI (HVAC), AED (electrical), or construction/industrial distribution events.',
  '{"event_name":"Home Delivery World USA 2026","event_url":"https://www.terrapinn.com/conference/home-delivery-world/index.stm","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"May 20-21, 2026","location":"Nashville, TN","cost":"Exhibition free to attend; booth costs typically $15k-$40k","venue":"Music City Center","description":"Home Delivery World USA 2026 is a premier conference and exhibition focused on retail logistics, e-commerce fulfillment, and last-mile delivery. Co-located with The Middle Mile, this 14-year running event covers the entire supply chain journey from warehouse to final customer delivery, including drayage, warehousing, inventory management, fulfillment, routing, dispatch, last-mile delivery, and returns.","industry_vertical":"supply_chain_and_distribution","exhibitor_mix":"Logistics providers (AIT Worldwide Logistics, Penske, J.B. Hunt, OneRail), technology companies (warehouse automation, robotics, AI-powered logistics, route optimization software, tracking systems), delivery service providers (last-mile carriers, autonomous delivery vehicles, electric fleet vehicles, drone technology), 3PLs, packaging solutions providers, freight management platforms, and e-commerce logistics technology vendors. Over 300+ exhibitors from across the e-commerce and logistics spectrum.","audience_mix":"Professionals from e-commerce, retail logistics, and supply chain sectors including retailers (Target, Wayfair, Williams-Sonoma, 7-Eleven, Kroger, IKEA), manufacturers, grocers, logistics managers, supply chain directors, distribution center operators, technology providers, delivery service managers, and transportation professionals. Typically draws 2,000-5,000 attendees with 250+ expert speakers.","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Comprehensive information found. Event features 100+ sessions, 75 startups, and 250+ speakers. Rated as Platinum tier conference by industry analysts. Exhibition is free to attend for attendees, with booth costs for exhibitors ranging $15k-$40k.","original_event_name":"Home Delivery World 2026","original_event_url":"https://www.terrapinn.com/conference/home-delivery-world/index.stm","added_to_master":"2026-04-27T14:51:36.965613","master_id":47,"overall_score":4.1,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":3,"rationale":"Event focuses heavily on last-mile delivery, e-commerce fulfillment, and retail logistics optimization. This is asset-light 3PL, freight forwarding, and logistics technology space - not core InstaLILY verticals. While supply chain adjacent, the event does not serve InstaLILY target industries: construction supply, industrial parts, healthcare/pharma, automotive goods, or food supply distributors. E-commerce fulfillment and last-mile delivery represent different operational models than multi-branch distributors and field service operations InstaLILY targets."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":6,"rationale":"Audience includes logistics managers, supply chain directors, and distribution center operators - roles adjacent to InstaLILY target functions. However, buyer mix skews toward e-commerce retailers (Target, Walfair, Kroger) and 3PLs rather than B2B distributors and field service operations. These attendees prioritize fulfillment velocity and last-mile execution rather than sales enablement, quoting, or field technician workflows that InstaLILY solves."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":7,"rationale":"Major annual US event in 2026 with 2,000-5,000 attendees, 250+ speakers, and strong industry reputation (Platinum tier). Nashville location accessible to US sales team. May timing works within planning calendar. However, e-commerce/retail logistics focus means attendee quality for InstaLILY targeting is diluted despite overall event scale."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":4,"rationale":"Mix of logistics managers, supply chain directors, and some C-suite retail/manufacturer leaders. However, the predominant attendee base skews toward logistics operations and technology roles rather than executive decision-makers at distributor or field service organizations. Lower concentration of sales leadership, procurement executives, or operations VPs at B2B distributors compared to pure supply chain/logistics roles."}},"reasoning":"Home Delivery World USA is a large, well-established supply chain event with strong execution in the last-mile logistics and e-commerce fulfillment space. However, it represents poor strategic fit for InstaLILY. The event serves asset-light 3PLs, freight forwarders, last-mile carriers, and e-commerce retailers - none of which are InstaLILY target verticals. InstaLILY solves for B2B distributors (construction, industrial parts, healthcare, automotive, food supply) and field service operations that need sales enablement, quoting automation, parts validation, and exception handling. Home Delivery World attendees operate in fundamentally different business models with different pain points (fulfillment speed, delivery optimization, warehouse robotics) rather than sales velocity, tribal knowledge, or multi-location branch management. While some supply chain functions overlap, the vertical misalignment and buyer functional mismatch make this a low-priority event for resource investment.","sales_brief":"Low priority event for InstaLILY. While scale and timing are strong, vertical misalignment is critical - event serves e-commerce/3PL/last-mile logistics, not B2B distributors or field service operations. Attendees optimize for fulfillment and delivery, not sales enablement or quoting. Risk of wasted booth spend and poor lead quality. Better resource allocation exists in verticals like HARDI (HVAC), AED (electrical), or construction/industrial distribution events."}'::jsonb
) on conflict (id) do update set
  event_name = excluded.event_name, event_url = excluded.event_url,
  normalized_event_url = excluded.normalized_event_url, dates = excluded.dates,
