  '6d4e9291-21d4-5ca3-9f92-020b6dd51470',
  'Total Supply Chain Summit London',
  'https://totalsupplychainsummit.co.uk/',
  'totalsupplychainsummit.co.uk',
  'April 28-29, 2026',
  '2026-04-28',
  '2026-04-29',
  'London Stansted, UK',
  'Radisson Blu Hotel London Stansted (also referenced as Radisson Red Hotel & Conference Centre Heathrow in some sources)',
  'Free for delegates',
  'A focused business summit bringing together senior supply chain and logistics professionals with leading solution providers through pre-arranged one-to-one meetings, expert seminars, and networking opportunities designed to explore innovative solutions for global supply chain challenges.',
  'supply_chain_and_distribution',
  'Supply chain solution providers, logistics technology companies, warehousing and transport providers, software vendors, and consulting firms serving the supply chain industry',
  'C-level executives, operations directors, procurement heads, logistics managers, and senior decision-makers from manufacturing, retail, logistics, and technology sectors with direct budgetary authority. Typically 60+ supply chain professionals attend each event.',
  'enriched',
  4.2,
  'While buyer seniority and functional alignment are strong, this event suffers from poor geographic accessibility for US sales team, very small scale (60 attendees), and misaligned vertical focus. Event serves European supply chain infrastructure rather than the North American distributor and manufacturer base that represents InstaLILY core ICP. International location and limited attendee pool make resource investment unjustifiable despite decision-maker quality.',
  'Pass on this event. While senior buyers attend, the 60-person London audience, European supply chain focus, and geographic distance make this poor ROI for US-based sales team. Audience skews toward 3PLs and logistics operators, not the distributor/manufacturer verticals where InstaLILY has proven success.',
  '{"event_name":"Total Supply Chain Summit London","event_url":"https://totalsupplychainsummit.co.uk/","source":"enriched","needs_enrichment":true,"dates":"April 28-29, 2026","location":"London Stansted, UK","cost":"Free for delegates","venue":"Radisson Blu Hotel London Stansted (also referenced as Radisson Red Hotel & Conference Centre Heathrow in some sources)","description":"A focused business summit bringing together senior supply chain and logistics professionals with leading solution providers through pre-arranged one-to-one meetings, expert seminars, and networking opportunities designed to explore innovative solutions for global supply chain challenges.","industry_vertical":"supply_chain_and_distribution","exhibitor_mix":"Supply chain solution providers, logistics technology companies, warehousing and transport providers, software vendors, and consulting firms serving the supply chain industry","audience_mix":"C-level executives, operations directors, procurement heads, logistics managers, and senior decision-makers from manufacturing, retail, logistics, and technology sectors with direct budgetary authority. Typically 60+ supply chain professionals attend each event.","enriched":true,"enrichment_success":true,"enrichment_notes":"Event is free for delegates to attend with complimentary lunch and refreshments. The summit features curated one-to-one meetings between buyers and suppliers, seminars, and networking sessions. Virtual attendance options are also available.","original_event_name":"Total Supply Chain Summit London","original_event_url":"https://totalsupplychainsummit.co.uk/","added_to_master":"2026-04-30T12:08:52.586292","master_id":50,"overall_score":4.2,"scores":{"supply_chain_vertical_alignment":{"score":4,"rationale":"Event targets broad supply chain professionals across multiple verticals including manufacturing, retail, and logistics. While it includes some 3PLs and logistics operators, the audience mix is too generalized and skews toward European logistics infrastructure providers rather than InstaLILY target verticals of distributors, manufacturers, and field service operations in construction, industrial parts, healthcare, automotive, or food supply."},"buyer_functional_alignment":{"score":8,"rationale":"Strong concentration of C-level executives, operations directors, and procurement heads with direct budgetary authority. These are decision-making roles aligned with InstaLILY buyer personas. However, the functional mix is broader than ideal, including general supply chain visibility seekers rather than execution-focused operations buyers."},"event_scale_timing":{"score":3,"rationale":"Event is in 2026 which passes timing check, but location is London, UK with limited accessibility for US sales team. Small event format (60+ attendees) is significantly below InstaLILY investment threshold. International logistics-focused audience reduces relevance for US-centric distributor and manufacturer ICP."},"buyer_seniority":{"score":8,"rationale":"Explicitly targets C and D-level executives with direct budgetary authority. Free attendance model attracts serious decision-makers. Curated one-to-one meeting format indicates high-intent, senior buyer participation. Strong concentration of purchase authority."}},"reasoning":"While buyer seniority and functional alignment are strong, this event suffers from poor geographic accessibility for US sales team, very small scale (60 attendees), and misaligned vertical focus. Event serves European supply chain infrastructure rather than the North American distributor and manufacturer base that represents InstaLILY core ICP. International location and limited attendee pool make resource investment unjustifiable despite decision-maker quality.","sales_brief":"Pass on this event. While senior buyers attend, the 60-person London audience, European supply chain focus, and geographic distance make this poor ROI for US-based sales team. Audience skews toward 3PLs and logistics operators, not the distributor/manufacturer verticals where InstaLILY has proven success."}'::jsonb
) on conflict (id) do update set
